    // Part 1 — pazandachilik darsiga yozilish
    private static ListeningPart ListenT8P1() => new(1,
        "You will hear a man phoning a cookery school to book an evening class.",
        [
            F("Megan", "Hello, Harbourside Cookery School, Megan speaking."),
            M("Daniel", "Hi. I'm calling about your evening cookery classes. I'd like to book one for my wife and me. It's a present for our wedding anniversary."),
            F("Megan", "How lovely. Did you have a particular class in mind?"),
            M("Daniel", "Well, we both love Italian food, so I was hoping for the Italian pasta class."),
            F("Megan", "I'm sorry, that one's fully booked until the end of next month. It's always the most popular. But we do have places on our Moroccan class, which couples really enjoy. You'd make a slow-cooked tagine, some flatbreads and a simple dessert."),
            M("Daniel", "Moroccan... Actually, that sounds great. We've never tried cooking it at home. Let's go for that."),
            F("Megan", "Good choice. That class runs on Tuesday and Thursday evenings. Tuesday's full next week, but there's still room on Thursday."),
            M("Daniel", "Thursday suits us better anyway."),
            F("Megan", "It starts at half past six, and it's three hours long. It used to be two and a half hours, but people said they felt rushed, so we added an extra half hour."),
            M("Daniel", "And how many people are there in a class? We'd rather it wasn't too crowded."),
            F("Megan", "We never have more than twelve. The kitchen has six cooking stations, and each pair shares one."),
            M("Daniel", "That sounds perfect. And what's the price?"),
