    // Part 3 — xotira bo'yicha psixologik tajriba
    private static ListeningPart ListenT9P3() => new(3,
        "You will hear two psychology students, Priya and Josh, discussing the report on their experiment on memory.",
        [
            M("Josh", "Hi, Priya. I've put all the results into the spreadsheet, so I thought we could plan the report."),
            F("Priya", "Great. Let's start with the introduction. We need to explain why we chose to study the testing effect."),
            M("Josh", "Well, the honest reason is that it's useful to us. We're both students, and if testing yourself really works better than rereading your notes, it should change the way we revise."),
            F("Priya", "True. And we can't claim that nobody's studied it before. There are dozens of studies on it. But that's fine, because we're repeating a classic experiment."),
            M("Josh", "Let's remind ourselves of the design. Sixty participants studied a list of thirty words. Half of them read the list three more times, and the other half tested themselves by writing down as many words as they could remember. Then a week later they all came back for a final recall test."),
            F("Priya", "Except that not all of them came back. That was our biggest problem. Finding volunteers at the start was easy, but only forty-four of the sixty returned for the second session."),
            M("Josh", "At least none of them were psychology students, so they didn't know what we were testing. We should still mention the drop-out in the limitations section, though."),
            F("Priya", "Definitely. And the results were pretty clear. The self-testing group recalled about forty per cent more words after a week, which is what we predicted. What surprised me was the confidence ratings. When we asked people how well they thought they'd do, the rereading group were much more confident than the testing group, and yet they remembered less."),
            M("Josh", "I suppose rereading feels easy, so people think they've learnt the material."),
            F("Priya", "Now, the weaknesses. I've been thinking about the week between the two sessions. We told people not to study the words, but we had no way of knowing whether they did."),
            M("Josh", "That's a real problem. Some of them might have written the list down and practised at home. The word list itself seemed about right, though. Nobody got everything correct, and nobody got nothing."),
            F("Priya", "And the room was quiet, so that's fine. How should we present the main results? I was going to use a line graph."),
            M("Josh", "I'm not sure. A line graph suggests change over time, and we've only got two separate groups. A table would be clear, but it's a bit dull."),
            F("Priya", "So a bar chart, then. One bar for each group, with the error bars shown."),
            M("Josh", "Yes, that's the best option. Then, in the discussion, who do we think our findings matter most for? I'd started writing about teachers."),
            F("Priya", "Teachers, possibly, but we didn't test anything in a classroom. And I suppose people who design learning apps might be interested, but that's a bit of a stretch. What we actually showed is about individual learners. I think it's most relevant to students preparing for exams."),
            M("Josh", "You're right. The message is: stop rereading and start testing yourself. And Dr Hughes wants us to suggest a follow-up study. I was thinking we could just repeat it with more people, or maybe use a longer gap, like a month."),
            F("Priya", "A bigger sample would be more reliable, but it's not very original, and with a month's gap we'd lose even more participants. What about testing whether the effect works for pictures as well as words? Lots of subjects, like biology or geography, involve remembering diagrams and maps."),
            M("Josh", "Good idea. Let's suggest that. Now, before we submit, let's make a checklist. The appendix needs a blank copy of the consent form that participants signed."),
            F("Priya", "Yes. And we need to watch the length. The word limit is 3,000 words, and at the moment we're way over."),
            M("Josh", "That doesn't include the references or the appendix, remember. And we have to submit it through the department's online portal. Not by email. Dr Hughes was very clear about that."),
            F("Priya", "OK. I'll start cutting the introduction tonight."),
        ],
        [
